@NODE Processor "ENVIRONLIB"

@{fg shine}Statement: Processor@{fg text}
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modes  : 
Syntax : Processor 

The function Processor returns the type of processor in the computer on 
which the program is currently running.

0 = 68000
1 = 68010
2 = 68020
3 = 68030
4 = 68040

See also @{"ProcessorFPU" link ProcessorFPU}

@ENDNODE Processor

@NODE ProcessorFPU "ENVIRONLIB"

@{fg shine}Statement: ProcessorFPU@{fg text}
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modes  : 
Syntax : ProcessorFPU

The function ProcessorFPU returns the type of floating point unit (FPU) in the computer on 
which the program is currently running.

0 = none
1 = 68881
2 = 68882
3 = 68040 (integrated)
4 = 68060 (integrated)

See also @{"Processor" link Processor}

@ENDNODE ProcessorFPU


@NODE ExecVersion "ENVIRONLIB"

@{fg shine}Statement: ExecVersion@{fg text}
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modes  : 
Syntax : ExecVersion 

The function ExecVersion returns the relevant information about the system the program is running on.

33 = 1.2
34 = 1.3
36 = 2.0 (preview)
37 = 2.0 
38 = 2.1 (only updated workbench)
39 = 3.0
40 = 3.1
44 = 3.5 (only updated workbench)
45 = 3.9 (only updated workbench)
46 = 3.1.4
47 = 3.2

50 = 4.0 (preview1)
51 = 4.0 (preview2-4)
52 = 4.0 (final)
53 = 4.1
54 = 4.2


@ENDNODE ExecVersion

@Node KickVersion "ENVIRONLIB"

  @{b}@{u}KickVersion@{ub}@{uu}

    @{b}Syntax@{ub}   : @{i}rc.w @{ui}= KickVersion
               @{i}rc.b @{ui}= KickVersion(Ver)

    @{b}Function@{ub} : Used to get or check Exec version.

    @{b}Values@{ub}   : If @{b}Ver@{ub} is specified it will return @{fg highlight}True@{fg text} if your Kickstart revision  is
               at   least   equal   to   @{b}Ver@{ub},  and  @{fg highlight}False@{fg text}  otherwise.  For  instance,
               @{fg highlight}KickVersion@{fg text}(37) checks whether you're running with  Kickstart  version
               37 or greater (i.e., AmigaDOS 2.04 and above).

               If @{b}Ver@{ub} is not specified, the version of Exec is returned.

    @{b}Example@{ub}  : @{fg highlight}If KickVersion@{fg text}(39)
                  @{fg highlight}Printf@{fg text} "OS 3.0 rulez\n"
               @{fg highlight}Else
                  Printf@{fg text} "Exec version is only %d... a bit old humm??!\n",@{fg highlight}KickVersion
               EndIf@{fg text}
@EndNode


@NODE VBRcheck "ENVIRONLIB"

@{fg shine}Statement: VBRcheck@{fg text}
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modes  : 
Syntax : test_vbr.b = VBRcheck
Require: 68010+ cpu 

Checks if the VBR-register has been moved to FAST-RAM.

@ENDNODE VBRcheck

@NODE VBRclear "ENVIRONLIB"

@{fg shine}Statement: VBRclear@{fg text}
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modes  : 
Syntax : VBRclear
Require: 68010+ cpu 

If the VBR register has been moved to FAST-RAM, it will be restored to be at start of CHIP-RAM.
The success will be returns as True.

@ENDNODE VBRclear

@NODE VBRmove "ENVIRONLIB"

@{fg shine}Statement: VBRmove@{fg text}
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modes  : 
Syntax : VBRmove
Require: 68010+ cpu 

Checks if the VBR-register has been moved to FAST-RAM and if not, moves the register vector to FAST-RAM.
The success will be returns as True.

@ENDNODE VBRmove



